{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false},"description":"Classifies the import table of one local ELF, PE/COFF or Mach-O image against a versioned, BinSight-authored capability taxonomy, reporting capability classes (for example process creation, process injection, executable-memory allocation, socket and HTTP networking, cryptographic API use, filesystem writes, registry access, service persistence, debugger detection, privilege and token changes, input hooking, screen capture) each as imports consistent with a behavior, never as proof it occurs or is reachable. Returns each capability with a confidence tier, the supporting imports (bounded by max_support with coverage), the taxonomy_version, the examined import count, and whether runtime symbol resolution (GetProcAddress/dlsym and similar) is imported. Reads imports once (file up to 256 MiB) WITHOUT executing the target, without network access and without writing files; the report is bounded to 8 MiB. Imports resolved dynamically are not classified; an absent capability means no matching import was observed, not that the behavior is impossible. Non-executable bytes receive a typed unsupported-target failure.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"examples":[{"path":"/artifacts/application"},{"max_support":32,"path":"/artifacts/application","slice":"arm64"}],"properties":{"max_support":{"default":16,"description":"Maximum supporting imports listed per capability before truncation","maximum":64,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"path":{"description":"Absolute filesystem path to the selected local file","minLength":1,"pattern":"^[^\\x00]*$","type":"string"},"slice":{"description":"Architecture of the Mach-O universal slice to analyze; defaults to the first declared slice","enum":["x86","x86_64","arm","arm64","powerpc"],"type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"},"name":"classify_impor